#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""blahaj - disassemble Perfect Dark stage setup files into decomp-style C.

Turns a setup file (UsetupXZ / Ump_setupXZ, 1173-compressed or raw, pulled
from a ROM or given as a file) into a src/setups/<name>.c in the shape the
decomp writes them - props/intro/paths/ailists as the props.h, intro.h and
commands.h macros - so tools/mksetups can build it straight back.

Everything about the file format comes from the tree, not from this script:

  - the record layouts are the macros in src/include/props.h, intro.h and
    commands.h, expanded symbolically and run backwards (a macro that bakes a
    constant word is checked, a parameter word is solved for);
  - the aicmd operand lengths are g_CommandLengths[] in src/game/chrai.c, so
    every vanilla opcode can be stepped over even when no macro names it;
  - prop record lengths come from the macros, with OBJ_LENGTHS below for the
    types no macro covers (cross-checked against port/include/preprocess/setup.h);
  - names come from src/include/constants.h, src/generated/<romid>/, and, for
    a stage the decomp already has, from src/setups/<name>.c itself.

What it cannot express it emits raw, never guesses: a prop record the macro
cannot reproduce byte for byte becomes a raw u32 run with a comment, an aicmd
it cannot size (mod windows 0x0400/0x0800, GE-X's additions) turns the rest
of that list into offset-labelled raw bytes. Both rebuild byte-identical.

Usage, from the pd-fojo tree root:

    tools/blahaj UsetupdishZ                   # file on disk (raw or 1173)
    tools/blahaj --rom basedir/data/pd.ntsc-final.z64 UsetupdishZ
    tools/blahaj --rom pd.z64 --xdelta mod.xdelta UsetupdishZ   # patched rom
    tools/blahaj --rom pd.z64 --file-patch patches/UsetupdishZ.xdelta UsetupdishZ
    tools/blahaj ... -o src/setups/setupdish.c

Dev-side only: needs python3; xdelta3 only for the --xdelta/--file-patch
inputs (the same authoring dependency mksetups --patches has).
"""

